# No Code-Built UI

**Default:** Player-facing UI lives in prefabs under `Assets/_MonkoGame/Prefabs/UI/` (or the project's UI prefab folder). C# binds `[SerializeField]` refs and handles callbacks only.

## Before writing UI code — STOP

| Task | Do this | Never do this |
|------|---------|---------------|
| New screen/modal | Unity MCP → prefab → thin `*View.cs` | `new GameObject` + `AddComponent<Image\|Button\|TextMeshProUGUI>` in runtime |
| Redesign existing screen | Edit prefab via Unity MCP; migrate off builders | Extend `Build*ScreenAssets.cs` or add a new editor builder |
| Dynamic list (lobby rows, chat) | `Instantiate(_rowPrefab)` from an authored row prefab | Build row hierarchy in a loop from code |
| Dev-only overlay | Self-spawn per `editor-dev-only-systems` rule | Serialize a dev type on a shipped prefab |

**Litmus test:** if you are calling `AddComponent<Image|Button|TextMeshProUGUI|RawImage|*LayoutGroup>` to lay out a screen, modal, or panel, you are in the wrong workflow.

## Canonical examples (copy these)

| Good | Path |
|------|------|
| Thin view | `Assets/_MonkoGame/Scripts/Runtime/Presentation/Screens/LobbyScreenView.cs` |
| Row prefab + pool | `LobbyTableRow.cs` + `LobbyTableRow.prefab` |
| Screen prefab | `Assets/_MonkoGame/Prefabs/UI/LobbyScreen.prefab` |

## Legacy — do not copy or extend

| Bad (legacy) | Path |
|--------------|------|
| Procedural HUD | `Presentation/Overlays/HUDController.cs` |
| Procedural score rows | `Presentation/Screens/GameOverModalView.cs` (`BuildScoreRows`) |
| Editor screen builder | `Editor/BuildLobbyScreenAssets.cs` |

Migrate when touched; never extend.

## Hard ban (runtime)

- `new GameObject` + `AddComponent<Image|Button|TextMeshProUGUI|RawImage|*LayoutGroup>` for screens, modals, or panels
- `Awake`/`Start` methods named `Build*`, `Create*Panel`, `Setup*UI` that author hierarchy
- Editor scripts that spawn RectTransforms, Images, Buttons, TMP, layout groups, or UIDocument trees to produce screen/modal prefabs

## Hard ban (editor)

- New `Build*Screen*.cs`, `Build*Modal*.cs`, `Build*Overlay*.cs`, or `*ScreenAssets*.cs` for player UI
- New `[MenuItem]` whose purpose is generating screen/modal UI hierarchy from code

Existing rebuild builders (`BuildLobbyScreenAssets`, `BuildCharacterSelectScreenAssets`, etc.) are legacy — do not add siblings.

## Allowed

- Thin `*View.cs` with `[SerializeField]` refs — logic, state, callbacks only
- **Unity MCP** to create/edit prefabs: `create_prefab`, `add_gameobject`, `add_ui_element`, `set_ui_text`, `set_rect_transform`, `add_ui_layout`
- Scene wiring that only `Instantiate`s existing prefabs and assigns serialized references
- Import/asset registration editor utilities (sprites, fonts, addressable groups) with no UI object creation
- **Dynamic list rows** via `Instantiate(_rowPrefab)` — the row prefab is authored in Editor/MCP
- Safe-area **infrastructure** (`FrostedPanel.CreateSafeAreaRoot`) — content still lives on the prefab under the safe-area child

## Workflow for a new or redesigned screen

1. Read the project's design spec / style guide for visual rules.
2. Build or edit the prefab through **Unity MCP** (or in Editor); screenshot and compare to reference.
3. Add/update the thin view script to bind serialized refs and handle user intent via callbacks.
4. Place a prefab instance in the scene and wire references on the orchestrator/bootstrap component.

## Agent checklist

- [ ] No new editor or runtime code that constructs screen/modal UI trees
- [ ] Prefab hierarchy created/edited via Unity MCP or Editor
- [ ] View scripts are thin — serialized refs + behavior only
- [ ] Dynamic content uses row prefab instances, not procedurally built panels
- [ ] Copied `LobbyScreenView` pattern, not `HUDController` or `BuildLobbyScreenAssets`
